Switch = An alternative to if-else statements for handling multiple conditions. More efficient for multiple conditions and fixed integer values.
Switches can also be used with char. 
The switch statement evaluates the expression and compares it with each case label.


Example: can be integers as well instead of characters
switch(operator) {
        case '+':
            result = num1 + num2;
            break;
        case '-':
            result = num1 - num2;
            break;
        case '*':
            result = num1 * num2;
            break;
        case '/':
            if (num2 == 0){
                printf("Can't divide by zero\n");
            }
            else {
               result = num1 / num2;
            }
            break;
        default:
            printf("Invalide operator or number\n");
    }
